      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. The original has several understandability issues:\n1. Uses `try/catch` instead of `assertThrows` — silently passes if no exception is thrown\n2. Uses `assertTrue(X.class.isInstance(e))` instead of the clearer `assertInstanceOf`\n3. Has multiple unused imports (`assertArrayEquals`, `assertEquals`, `assertNull`, `EncoderException`, `@Disabled`)\n4. Variable name `inputS` is cryptic\n\nLet me write the improved test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces the silent `try/catch` with `assertThrows` (ensuring the test fails if no exception is thrown), uses `assertInstanceOf` for clearer type checking, removes all unused imports, and adds descriptive comments explaining why `αβ` triggers the truncation scenario and what the expected failure mode is."
    }
